<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Junior Juz</h1><p class="st-meta">1718 CE – 1824 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western division of the Kazakhs, whose khan Abulkhair first accepted Russian protection in 1731.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tauke-khan">Tauke Khan's</a> death around 1718, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kazakh-khanate">Kazakh Khanate</a> split, with the Junior Juz holding the western steppe between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aral-sea">Aral Sea</a>, the Caspian and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Ural River</a>. Its tribes belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alimuly">Alimuly</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baiuly">Baiuly</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhetiru">Zhetiru</a> groupings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under pressure from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kalmyk-khanate">Kalmyk Khanate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abulkhair-khan">Abulkhair Khan</a> sought Russian protection, which was formalised in 1731. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orenburg">Orenburg</a> in 1743 as a trading and military base on its border. The juz was nomadic, raiding and trading with Russia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrym-datuly">Syrym Datuly</a> led a long revolt against both the khans and Russia from 1783.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Part of the Junior Juz formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bukey-horde">Bukey Horde</a> in 1801. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> abolished the khanship of the Junior Juz in 1824 and divided it into administrative districts, despite continuing resistance among its clans.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/junior-juz.jpg" alt="Junior Juz" width="320" height="180"><figcaption>Image: ru:User:Wassily · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%96%D1%83%D0%B7.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1718 CE – 1824 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abulkhair Khan, Nurali Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kazakh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Kazakhstan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lesser Horde, Little Zhuz, Kishi Juz</dd></dl></aside></div>
